# Backend base URL for direct API calls (BUILD-TIME variable — it is baked
# into the production bundle at `npm run build`; changing it requires a
# rebuild + redeploy).
#
# You have TWO supported topologies — pick ONE:
#
# 1) SAME-ORIGIN via the Cloudflare Worker proxy (RECOMMENDED, no config):
#    Leave this unset (''). The worker (cloudflare/worker.js) proxies
#    /api/*, /v1/* and /health server-to-server to the origin configured
#    via `ROUTELLM_API_ORIGIN` (wrangler secret) — the browser never talks
#    to the backend directly, so CORS and mixed content are non-issues.
#
#        # window: unset VITE_API_BASE_URL entirely
#
# 2) DIRECT CROSS-ORIGIN calls (no worker proxy):
#    Point this at the FastAPI backend origin. MUST be https:// in
#    production — a production build with an http:// value is demoted to
#    same-origin instead of shipping requests that browsers block as
#    mixed content. Also set CORS_ORIGINS on the backend to include this
#    dashboard origin.
#
#        VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.your-domain.com
#
# 3) Local dev: unset — the Vite dev proxy (vite.config.ts) forwards
#    /api, /v1 and /health to 127.0.0.1:8000.
#
# Cloudflare: set this in the Workers build environment variables (Build
# settings → Variables), then redeploy (`npm run deploy`).
